{green|Invisible Man}

Invisible People are inhabitants of the mysterious Quark Palace, a metallic, spherical structure surrounded by violet lightning. They are most likely the result of magical experiments. 

{gold|Special Abilities:}
{gold|Invisibility:} Hidden by their invisibility, they take only 10% of damage from regular attacks, but suffer double from magic. Facing them, the enemy strikes at nothing—until suddenly a blow comes out of nowhere.

creatures.new-monsters-pack.kurek-creatu:
{green|Cherub}

Cherubim in the are high in the hierarchy celestial beings who serve as guardians and protectors of divine holiness. Described as having many wings and great power and speed, they often appear in the visions of prophets, symbolizing glory and holy presence. With their great offensive and defensive power and flying ability, Cherubs are among the mightiest and fastest creatures among celestials. 

{gold|They do 150% damage when attacking devils and strengthen morale of allied units.}

 {#00aaff|Cherubim can 3 times resurrect allied units fallen on the battlefield, provided they were not undead in life.}

{green|Scholar}

Scholars have devoted much of their time to the study of things past, giving them much insight into events to come.
Scholars and lecturers train themselves to control and project their personal energistic forces, which they deliver as ranged blasts.
While scholars suffer the normal penalty for ranged unit hand-to-hand attack damage (50%), the better trained lecturers do not.

{gold|Special Abilities:}
 All Scholars grant their hero mastery of the Scholar’s art at the Expert level, a discipline passed down through generations of learned wanderers. With this gift, their hero can instantly share and exchange spells with any visiting ally, spreading hard-won knowledge as swiftly as spoken words.

{green|Squire}

 Squires and Men-at-Arms use flails that have a chance of stunning an opponent during attack. The chance and duration of stunning depends on the level of stun ability.

{gold|Special Abilities:}
 Basic Stun Attack: This creature's Stun ability gives it a 10% chance of stunning enemies when it attacks in melee combat. Stunned enemies cannot take any action or retaliate for one turn.

{green|Agar's Pet}

Agar's Pets are grotesque, flightless vultures created by the twisted warlock Agar. They could be considered a failed experiment, that was supposed to create cockatrices. These two-meter-tall abominations have bloated bodies, bat-like violet wings, and piercing red eyes capable of paralyzing their prey with a single gaze. 

 {gold|Special Abilities:}
 Melee attack with beak and claws. Paralysis gaze with 10% chance to occur. 99% magic damage immunity.

These annoying creatures are {#40bfff|99% immune to magic damage, but not immune to a good sword blow}. Though they cannot fly, they lurk in the darkness, waiting to strike with their sharp talons and terrifying beaks.

{green|Terrible Eye}

Terrible Eyes are the most powerful and terrifying beholders of the twisted warlock Agar. These massive, two-meter floating aberrations resemble grotesque brain-head with horns, a gaping maw, and a single, glowing magical eye of terror.  

{gold|Special Abilities:}
 Ranged magic beam attack. Flight. Casts randomly spells after attack. Unlimited shots. Free attack-they can shoot even if they are surrounded. Short attack range (10).

Unlike lesser beholders, Terrible Eyes unleash devastating spells upon attacking. Their magic beam may inflict {#40bfff|Charm, Fear,} {#00aaff|Berserk, Fireball, or Dispel Magic}, making them unpredictable and deadly foes. They dwell in the deepest underground caverns, waiting for their next victim.

{#ff0000|Lurker}

Lurkers are rare types of beholders, which were created by the twisted warlock Agar. Their familiar look might be deceiving, because they have been credited with different magic ingredients in order to gain different abilities from other types of evil eyes. 

{gold|Special Ability: Ranged magic missile attack. Flight. Casts negative spell after every attack.}

Unlike regular beholders, these aberrations can fly thanks to their antigravitational magic aura.
When lurkers attack, they shoot a dark magic energy bolt, which randomly casts a harmful spell on an enemy. The possible spells include: {#00aaff|Curse, Disrupting Ray, Slow, Sorrow, Weakness, Forgetfulness, Misfortune}, {#40bfff|Magic Leech, Cowardice, and Cancellation}.

{green|Black Gorgon}

The sturdy Black Demigorgons attack with their acidic breath.

{gold|Special Abilities:}
 The Black Gorgon has a death stare with a 10% chance per attack of killing 1 creature in a troop outright per 10 Black Gorgons.

It can also change its enemies to stone with their cursed gaze and is immune to poison and acid damage.

{green|Spectral Dragon}

No single type of dragon gives up its bones to form a Spectral Dragon. Instead, these fell beasts are composed of the bones of every breed of dragon, cunningly arranged into a single skeleton and infused with unlife by the sacrifice of a high-ranking Necromancer's soul.

{gold|Special Abilities:}
 Undead. Decreases enemy morale by -1. Casts Advanced Curse 100% before attack. Can cast dragon breath dark magic damage  Dragon.
Unlike the majority of dragons, Bone Dragons, Ghost Dragons and Spectral Dragons don't have long breath attack, i.e. they damage only the troops directly attacked by them. 
Spectral dragons have the ability to damage the body by dragon breath dark magic spell, or attack soul of their prey with Advanced Curse before every attack.

{green|Orange Dragon}

Any forest under the protection of an orange dragon is a calm and magical place, one best left alone if you're wise. Like the sprite, this creature is born magically, spawned by the forces of Nature from a clear pool of water.

{gold|Special Abilities:}
 Orange dragons are almost completely immune to magical attacks, reflecting spells back at the caster (70%, similar to the Magic Mirror spell). 

They can also cast spells such as Confusion, Fire Ring, Fireball, Lightning Bolt, Ice Bolt, Ice Ring, Inferno, Meteor Shower, Chain Lightning and Magic Arrow.

{green|Purple Dragon}

The purple dragon is a majestic creature with scales that shimmer like amethyst as it soars high in the skies. It is likely the oldest dragon species the world has ever seen.

{gold|Special Abilities:}
Its blue fiery breath covers a large area, leaving flames that burn longer than ordinary fire. These burns cannot be healed for 2 turns.

This dragon possesses a unique resistance to magic, protecting it from most spells.

{green|Hornet Drone}

The Hornet Drone is a unique and rare larger wasp, acting as a viceroy within the hive. Its commanding presence inspires nearby swarms, while its tactical prowess bolsters their ferocity in battle.

{gold|Special Abilities:}
{gold|Bloodlust:} The Hornet Drone can cast the Bloodlust spell on allied wasps, increasing their attack power and unleashing their full potential.

{green|Wasp Sentry}

The Wasp Sentry is a vigilant defender of the hive, always ready to protect its territory. Stronger and more aggressive than the Worker Wasp, it poses a significant threat to any intruder.

{gold|Special Abilities:}
{gold|Flight:} The Wasp Sentry's mobility makes it difficult to corner or strike effectively.
{gold|Venomous Sting (25% chance after attack):} Its sting has an increased chance to poison enemies, dealing damage over time.
{gold|Strike and Return:} The Wasp Sentry attacks swiftly and retreats, minimizing the risk of being surrounded.

{green|Wasp Worker}

Worker Wasps are the lowest rank in the wasp hierarchy, tasked with gathering resources and constructing the hive. Though not particularly strong, their perseverance and determination make them a challenging opponent.

{gold|Special Abilities:}
{gold|Flight:} The Worker Wasp uses its ability to fly, making it harder to hit in combat.
{gold|Venomous Sting (15% chance after attack):} After each attack, the Worker Wasp has a chance to poison the enemy, dealing additional damage over time.
{gold|Strike and Return:} After attacking, the Worker Wasp can quickly retreat to a safer distance, avoiding retaliation.

{green|Wild Griffin}

Wild Griffins are fierce, indomitable creatures, filled with raw strength and an unbreakable spirit. Unlike their tamed kin, they defy all attempts at control, their will as unyielding as mountain stone, and their hearts driven by ancient instincts.

{gold|Special Abilities:}
 In battle, Wild Griffins are skilled at countering attacks, striking fear into the hearts of their foes.
 Their blows are swift and precise, making them a daunting challenge for any who dare face them.

{green|Bloodeyed Cyclop}

Bloodeyed Cyclopes are fearsome shamanic warriors who channel fiery energy through their glowing red eyes.

{gold|Special Ability:}
 Their deadly eye beams incinerate enemies, dealing fire damage, and magically paralyze them with crimson energy, immobilizing them for a turn.

 Uniquely, they can use this beam effectively in close combat, where it can strike two units standing in a line. This makes them exceptionally versatile, both at range and in melee.

 As spiritual leaders of the cyclopes, they also possess the ability to cast the Misfortune spell, cursing their enemies with dreadful luck.

{green|Cyclops Warrior}

Fearless combatants who have abandoned throwing boulders in favor of melee combat with massive clubs.

{gold|Special Abilities:}
 Each of their strikes not only deals tremendous damage but also has a chance to stun the enemy, immobilizing them for one turn.

 Although they lack ranged attacks, they make up for it with exceptional resilience and devastating strength, making them unmatched in close-quarters battles. Their sheer brutality makes them a key unit for breaking through enemy lines.

